{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.55,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "bridged_nets",
      "components": ["R50", "R51"],
      "pins": ["R50.1", "R50.2", "R51.1", "R51.2"],
      "nets": ["I2C1_SCL_FCC", "I2C2_SDA_FCC", "I2C2_SCL_NAVC", "I2C2_SDA_NAVC"],
      "observed": "On the Connections sheet 'I2C Connections' block, the 0-ohm series link resistor R50 joins I2C1_SCL_FCC (FCC) to I2C2_SCL_NAVC (NAVC), but the second link resistor R51 joins I2C2_SDA_FCC (FCC) to I2C2_SDA_NAVC (NAVC). The two halves of the inter-MCU I2C link therefore sit on different FCC peripheral buses (SCL on I2C1, SDA on I2C2), and the link's SDA line is merged onto the FCC I2C2 peripheral bus that also carries the INA219, PCA9685 and FCC EEPROM.",
      "expected": "Both link lines must belong to the same FCC I2C controller. The NAVC sheet's own annotation states 'I2C2_NAVC already pulled up by I2C1_FCC resistors!', i.e. the intended link is FCC I2C1 (I2C1_SCL_FCC + I2C1_SDA_FCC) <-> NAVC I2C2. The SDA link line should be I2C1_SDA_FCC, not I2C2_SDA_FCC.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "Connections sheet, 'I2C Connections': R50 between 'I2C1_SCL_FCC' and (right) 'I2C2_SCL_NAVC'; R51 between 'I2C2_SDA_FCC' and (right) 'I2C2_SDA_NAVC'"},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "NAVC sheet note: 'I2C2_NAVC already pulled up by I2C1_FCC resistors!'"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "confirmed in Hades.sch: NAVC<->FCC run UART2 + I2C + GPIO between the two MCUs"}
      ],
      "impact": "The FCC<->NAVC I2C link cannot operate as a single bus because SCL is driven by the FCC I2C1 peripheral while SDA is driven by the FCC I2C2 peripheral; the navigation computer will not be reachable over I2C. In addition, tying the link SDA to I2C2_SDA_FCC merges the inter-MCU link with the FCC sensor/power bus (INA219/PCA9685/EEPROM), corrupting sensor and PWM-driver communication.",
      "confidence": 0.55
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The drawing is largely consistent with the specification (the barometer RESET/EOC swap and the redundant I2C2 pull-ups are documented, and the PCA9685's 0x41 strapping is internally coherent with its A0 tie to +3.3V), but the FCC<->NAVC I2C link block mismatches bus indices: the SCL line uses I2C1_FCC while the SDA line uses I2C2_FCC, which both breaks the inter-MCU I2C link and bridges it onto the FCC I2C2 peripheral bus."
}

